 algorithm","topics":[],"score":225725,"global_rank":143962},{"name":"snigdhakakkar/Twitter_Sentiment_Analysis_Engine","owner":"snigdhakakkar","html_url":"https://github.com/snigdhakakkar/Twitter_Sentiment_Analysis_Engine","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Jupyter Notebook","description":"Twitter is one of the widely used social media platforms. Many a times, we see strong discussion on Twitter about someone\u2019s opinion that sometimes results in a collection of negative tweets. For gauging whether the kind of tweets are positive, negative or have a neutral sentiment, we can use this simple Twitter Sentiment Analysis Engine. Sentiment analysis is a task of natural language processing. Various social media platforms monitor the sentiments of those engaged in a discussion using such sentiment analysis engines. For the purpose of this project, I have used a Kaggle dataset about a long discussion within a group of users on Twitter. Our task was to identify how many tweets are negative and positive so that we can give a conclusion.","topics":[],"score":225725,"global_rank":143963},{"name":"snigdhakakkar/House_Price_Predictor","owner":"snigdhakakkar","html_url":"https://github.com/snigdhakakkar/House_Price_Predictor","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Jupyter Notebook","description":"Steps Implemented:  79 initial features Technologies: Python, NLTK, Keras, Scikit-learn, pandas, Numpy Pre-processed the raw data, handled the missing values and applied feature engineering Used hyperparameter optimization techniques to find the optimum parameters Predicted Sale Prices to minimize the Cost function using Machine learning Regression models & Neural Networks Explored Linear regression with regularization methods (Ridge, LASSO etc.) & XgBoost Model using scikit-learn","topics":[],"score":225725,"global_rank":143964},{"name":"snigdhakakkar/Corona-Virus-Covid-19-Live-tracking-India","owner":"snigdhakakkar","html_url":"https://github.com